course: dictionary
lesson: 3858
title: One word, two meanings
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: A word can have more than one meaning. The dictionary gives two meanings for fox: as a noun it is an animal, and as a verb it means to confuse or trick someone. Context tells you which one is meant. Ask yourself whether the word is naming a thing or doing an action.
explain: «Arctic foxes have small ears, short legs and short noses that lose little heat.» Here fox is a noun, because ears, legs and noses belong to the animal. Now try this: «The puzzle foxed me for an hour.» Here foxed is a verb, and it means confused, so the puzzle confused me for an hour. The words around the word show its job.
explain: Check your meaning by swapping it into the sentence. If you put the animal meaning into «The puzzle ___ me for an hour», it makes no sense, so you know the verb meaning is right. Endings change a word too: foxes is the plural of fox, and foxed is the past tense of the verb.
fact: A fox is a wild animal of the dog family, with a pointed nose, pointed ears, reddish fur and a long bushy tail.
fact: A female fox is called a vixen, and a baby fox is called a cub or kit.
fact: To fox someone means to confuse or trick them.
fact: Foxes are mostly active at night (nocturnal) and live in dens; many also live in cities in the UK, Ireland and Australia.
fact: Never feed or touch a wild fox.
exercise: «Owls, foxes, cats, weasels, snakes and hawks all hunt mice.» In this sentence, what is a fox? | A kind of owl | To trick someone | *An animal that hunts mice | A type of bin
exercise: What is the name for a female fox? | Kit | Den | *Vixen | Cub
exercise: Jade says, «He tried to fox me with a tricky riddle.» What does fox mean here? | To run very fast | *To confuse or trick | A wild animal with a bushy tail | To eat quickly
test: In «The fox crept past the bins at night», what is fox? | A type of bin | *An animal, the noun | A colour | To trick someone
test: Which is the plural of fox? | Foxs | Foxies | Vixens | *Foxes
exam: In «Don't let the clever salesman fox you with his words», what does fox mean? | *To confuse or trick | A wild dog-family animal | A female animal | A den for sleeping
